# Cached API data and any local secrets stay out of the repo (CLAUDE.md security).
# Three exceptions, and they are exceptions because they CANNOT BE REBUILT:
#   availability/ — snapshots of who was hurt, capturable only live (the players
#     table holds no history), so a lost snapshot is lost forever;
#   ledger/       — the published record every accountability claim rests on;
#   sent.jsonl    — who has already been mailed; losing it double-sends to
#     paying subscribers.
# These previously lived only in a GitHub Actions cache, which is evicted after
# 7 days without access — and the Tuesday run touches sent.jsonl on exactly a
# 7-day cycle. The registry stays ignored: it holds addresses, and run/sync.py
# rebuilds it from Stripe, so it is recoverable.
data/*
!data/raw/
data/raw/*
!data/raw/availability/
!data/processed/
data/processed/*
!data/processed/ledger/
!data/processed/sent.jsonl
# flock artifacts are transient, never part of the record
data/processed/ledger/**/*.lock
.env
.env.*

# Per-subscriber output (personal league data; the registry itself is under data/)
reports/subscribers/
# Dry-run drafts: real subscriber addresses and their personalised reports.
reports/outbox/
# Generated reports name real league members (rival, opponent, waiver rivals).
# The anonymised public demo is site/sample-report.html, built through
# render.report.anonymize_for_public(); these raw renders must not be tracked.
reports/rival-report-*.html
reports/rival-report-*.txt
# The legacy league demo pair (`make demo`) — same reason, same names.
reports/league-demo-public.html

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# Local Claude Code session settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# nflverse CSVs are large and re-fetchable; cached like the rest of data/raw/.
data/raw/nflverse/
